<!-- FAQ -->
<section id="faq" class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> FAQ</div>
      <h2 style="margin-top:18px">Questions, <span class="accent">answered</span>.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">How complex can my strategy be?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">As complex as you can describe. Elliott wave counts with Fibonacci targets and hard invalidation levels, smart money concepts — liquidity sweeps, break of structure, change of character, order blocks, fair value gaps — Wyckoff phases, harmonic patterns, divergences, squeezes, any indicator on any timeframe. Then layer on the economic and earnings calendars, intermarket lead-lag, statistical spreads and volatility regimes, with event blackouts, scaling in and out, pyramiding and trailing stops. If you can say it in plain English, the AI can build it.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">Is there anything it can't build yet?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">Your algo works from live and historical prices, every technical indicator, and the economic and earnings calendars — so anything expressed in those terms is fair game. That includes smart money concepts: order blocks, fair value gaps and liquidity sweeps are all read from the candles, not from raw exchange depth. Three things are out of scope for now: strategies that read the live order book, strategies that need to know what is already sitting in your account (portfolio rebalancing, for example), and strategies that depend on an outside dataset we don't carry yet. More data sources are on the way.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">Do I need to know how to code?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">No. You describe your strategy in plain language and the AI structures it into a working algo — the exact entry and exit rules. You never touch code.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">What's the difference between an algo and a bot?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">An algo is just the rules that produce your entry and exit levels. A bot bundles fixed volume and leverage into one rigid package. AlgoBuild builds algos — so position size and risk always stay in your hands.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">How is my position size decided?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">You decide. Set a leverage per position, or a fixed risk amount for if the price reaches your exit level. Either method calculates the precise volume for every trade — the algo only ever defines where to enter and exit.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">Can I run it on my own broker or exchange?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">Yes. Connect your account and your algo executes automatically the moment its rules trigger — no manual trading. You can also share it on the network if you want others to run it too.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">Is my strategy kept confidential?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">Yes. Anyone you share it with sees the track record — win rate, drawdown, equity curve — never the underlying rules. Your logic never leaves the platform.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">What happens before my algo goes live?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">The AI backtests it over years on its entry and exit levels, then runs a live forward test. Only strategies that clear strict quality bars are cleared to run.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq" data-reveal>
        <summary><span class="q">Can I edit my strategy after creating it?</span><span class="ico"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span></summary>
        <div class="a">Yes. You can edit your strategy anytime and rebuild the updated version.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

